  "term": "intimate partner violence",
  "definition": "Intimate partner violence is abuse within a close relationship, such as between current or former spouses or dating partners. It involves a pattern of assault and controlling behavior that can include physical, psychological, or sexual harm, as well as intimidation, stalking, isolation, deprivation, or reproductive coercion.",
